# Atlas Evolution 0.13.0
> A Hermes plugin that learns from repeat tool failures. 28,226 lines of Python, MIT licence. Colours: green = carries over to Nimbalyst, yellow = carries over with a gap, red = Hermes only. Status on each "Nimbalyst fit" node: done = built and merged into the fork's main (merge commit be28396f8, PR #2; first build 9769852b2, review fixes f39b25dc5), todo = not built, question = open. Updated 2026-11-24.

## 1 Signals {color: yellow}
> Collects what goes wrong. Nimbalyst stores every tool call in ai_agent_messages.
- Hooks it listens to {tags: hermes}
  - post_tool_call: failed tool calls
  - pre_llm_call and post_llm_call: turn timing
  - post_api_request and api_request_error
  - on_session_end, on_session_finalize
  - on_skill_lifecycle: skill use
  - subagent_start, post_compaction
- What it records
  - Tool name
  - One of 22 failure classes
  - Short detail
  - Owner corrections
- 14-day history replay seeds the first pass
- Modules: signals, logwatch, backfill, telemetry, operations
- Nimbalyst fit {color: green, status: done}
  > Built: the tool get_tool_failures (sessionContextServer.ts) reads ai_agent_messages through toolFailures.ts. Three buckets: blocked, broken-tool, habit. Seven habit classes. Codex rows have their own pairing, with codex: keys.
  - Not carried over: turn timing, API errors, skill use, owner corrections {status: todo}

## 2 Lessons {color: green}
> The core idea. A repeat failure becomes a short "when X, do Y" rule.
- Rule: 3+ hits on 2+ days or sessions
- Fixed templates per failure class
- Reflector: a model drafts lessons with no template
  - Drafts always wait for the owner
- Modes
  - auto: goes live after 2 hits in the owner's own turns
  - otherwise: waits as a candidate
- Lesson record (experience.py:63)
  - signature, tool, klass, hint, origin, status, text
  - shown, hints, verdict, rate_before, rate_after
  - baseline_failures, baseline_calls
- Modules: lessons, reflector, hints, packs
- Nimbalyst fit {color: green, status: done}
  > Built as step 5 of the evolution-pass skill: a habit key with 3+ hits on 2+ days and no lesson becomes a live lesson in lessons.json. Days only: Atlas also counts 2+ sessions; the spec chose days on purpose. The agent writes the text; it goes live at once, with no owner wait. Codex keys get no lesson. Not run yet.

## 3 Delivery {color: yellow}
> How the agent sees active lessons.
- Prompt section, 1,400 characters at most
- Hint added to a failing tool result (tool_hints on)
- Optional agent tool: hermes_atlas_evolution_lessons
- Nimbalyst fit {color: yellow, status: done}
  > Built: a section between evolution:lessons markers in the Claude Code MEMORY.md, 1,400 characters at most, beside the memory-spike learn section.
  - Gap: a session in another folder or worktree may load a different MEMORY.md {status: question}
  - Gap: Codex sessions get no lessons until registerContextProvider works (ExtensionLoader.ts:1026) {status: todo}
  - Gap: no hint on a failing tool result {status: todo}

## 4 Measurement {color: green}
> Checks whether each change helped.
- Lesson verdict: 14 days before vs 14 days after
  - effective, ineffective, inconclusive
  - auto mode retires an ineffective lesson
- Change experiments: 7 days before vs after
  - config edits, skill edits
- Not yet tested over weeks of real use
- Modules: experiments, evolve, insights, evolution_index
- Nimbalyst fit {color: green, status: done}
  > Built: evaluateHabitKeys in toolFailures.ts. Inconclusive below 20 calls or 5 before-failures; effective at half the rate; ineffective at 0.9 times the rate with 3+ failures. The skill judges at day 15 to day 45 and retires an ineffective lesson.
  - Not carried over: change experiments for config and skill edits {status: todo}
  - Kill check: fewer than 2 final verdicts after 30 days means review the thresholds {status: question}

## 5 Proposals {color: green}
> Anything bigger than a lesson waits for the owner.
- Each has risk, evidence, exact command
- Only the owner approves, in a terminal
  - Refuses when an agent marker is set
- Plugin runs only lessons, skill_lock, some environment fixes
- Every action logged with an undo
- skill_rollback opens when a skill change regressed
- Modules: proposals, decisions, explain
- Nimbalyst fit {color: green, status: done}
  > Built: tracker items "Clarify block message", "Fix tool setup" and "Lesson did not help". The filed list in lessons.json stops a second item for the same key. A comment goes on an item after 14 quiet days; the owner closes it.

## 6 Schedule and cost {color: green}
- Autopilot pass about hourly
- Weekly digest cron job
- Self-cost meter per hook
- Modules: autopilot, selfcost, billing, report
- Nimbalyst fit {color: yellow, status: done}
  > Built: the skill's setup step creates a daily 06:00 automation "Evolution pass". It runs only while a Nimbalyst window is open on the workspace.
  - Not carried over: cost meter and weekly digest {status: todo}

## 7 Storage {color: blue}
- evolution.sqlite3, schema 8
- settings.json
- 90-day retention
- Tables: lesson, change, proposal
- Nimbalyst {status: done}
  > One file per workspace: nimbalyst-local/evolution/lessons.json, with cursor, filed, passSessionIds, memoryDir and lessons. No new table.

## 8 Hermes upkeep {color: red}
> Hermes-only. Skip for Nimbalyst.
- guard: blocks commands that kill Hermes
- doctor, hermes_care, environment
- gateway repair, fleet_update, system_update
- memory_care: MEMORY.md and USER.md dedupe
- skill_health, radar
- ecosystem: Hermes plugin catalog
- Dashboard tab, menu, admin, cli, i18n

