## 10 Gap review 2026-11-24 {color: red}
> Two separate reviews (Sonnet and Fable 5.2; Mythos is not offered by this Nimbalyst build) of branch feat/evolution-loop at 9769852b2. "Both" = both reviewers found it. The lead checked each line marked checked in the code.
- Fix before the first run {status: done}
  > Fixed in commit f39b25dc5 on feat/evolution-loop (pushed). Gate: 16,700 tests passed, 26 skipped. Rule 1 resultText stays hand-written: the runtime package does not export subagentDrain.ts.
  - lessons.json saves only at the last step: a failed run files the same items again (both, checked, SKILL.md:65,83)
  - truncated turns on for any sample over 200 characters, so the "failures stopped" comment never runs (both, checked, toolFailures.ts:606)
  - automations_list and automations_create are not auto-allowed: setup waits on a prompt (both, checked, toolPolicy.ts)
  - Hook key: the [tag] rule searches the whole text and the 40-character fallback changes with numbers in the message (both, checked, toolFailures.ts:331)
  - A block seen once gets a tracker item; the spec target is 20 or more (both, checked, SKILL.md:48)
  - The skill never reads the clock, so "now" and "14 days back" can be wrong (Sonnet, checked, SKILL.md:60)
  - Rule 1: resultText repeats extractToolResultText (Sonnet, checked, subagentDrain.ts:46)
- First-run plan is wrong {status: done}
  > Fixed: the checklist now copies the real database into the dev app's folder and runs in the Nimbalyst workspace (commit 1c8415c18). Section 11 lists a new first-run gap.
  - dev:user2 reads its own empty database, so the run finds no failures (Fable, checked, dev-user2.mjs)
  - This workspace has few failures; Phoenix has about 9 times more (Fable, database query)
- Fix after the first run {status: todo}
  - The query loads every tool row with full text and no limit (both, checked, sessionContextServer.ts:171)
  - The after-window is a fixed 14 days, so judging again up to day 45 gives the same answer (Fable, checked, toolFailures.ts:868)
  - No per-tool call totals in the result (Fable)
  - Bash:exit-code and other keys get lessons that cannot help (both)
  - A misspelled tool name gets its own "Fix tool setup" item (Sonnet)
  - Lesson text goes into MEMORY.md with no clean-up of untrusted failure text (Sonnet, security)
- Atlas parts the spec dropped {status: question}
  - shown: whether a session loaded the lesson; without it the after-window mixes in sessions that never saw it (Sonnet)
  - Lesson expiry after quiet days, so the 1,400 characters do not fill (Fable)
  - Detail in the key, so one exit-code lesson does not cover every command (Fable)
  - Keep a lesson the owner reworded (Sonnet)
- Tracker {status: done}
  - NIL.6 to NIL.12 done after the merge. NIL.13 (first run) stays to-do.

## 11 Gap review 2 (2026-11-24) {color: red}
> Second pair of reviews (Sonnet and Fable 5.2; Mythos is not offered) of main at be28396f8, with section 10 excluded. The lead checked each line marked checked.
- Blocks learning {status: todo}
  - No daily home: the installed app (0.84.4) has no evolution extension, and dev:user2 reads a frozen copy, so no pass sees new sessions (Fable, checked) {status: done}
    > Owner chose: install a fork build. Branch sync/upstream-0.84.4 merges upstream 0.84.4 into the fork (13e2d8b35; gate: 19,431 tests passed, 30 skipped) and takes updates from CaptainMittens/nimbalyst, which has no releases (1e174c8ac). Built as release/mac-arm64/Nimbalyst.app. Install waits on the owner. Each upstream release needs a merge and a rebuild.
  - A lesson starts at 3 hits but a final verdict needs 5 before-failures, so a 3- or 4-hit lesson stays live and inconclusive forever and fills the 1,400 characters (Fable, checked, toolFailures.ts:736, SKILL.md:65) {status: done}
    > Owner chose: retire a lesson still inconclusive after day 45, with no tracker item (90897fa7f).
  - This workspace has 1 eligible habit key in 14 days (Bash:exit-code, 16 hits), so 5 final verdicts cannot happen here (Fable, database query)
- First run {status: todo}
  - Split state: the dev run writes the real lessons.json and MEMORY.md, but its tracker items stay in the database copy; `filed` then blocks the real items (Fable, checked) {status: done}
    > The checklist now backs up both files before the run and puts them back after it (975079fc5). With the fork build installed, the run can use the real database, and this gap goes away.
  - The 7 checks test plumbing only; none checks a count, a verdict or a run started by the automation (Fable)
  - Tip: add one lesson dated 16 days back, so the judging step runs (Fable)
- Bugs and risks {status: todo}
  - One deleted tracker item fails the comment call, and the stop rule then ends every later pass (Fable, SKILL.md:57,90)
  - "Grep is not available in this session" is 18 of 20 "No such tool" hits: a habit, filed as a broken tool (Fable, toolFailures.ts:394)
  - Lesson text goes live with no length or character check; Atlas allows 12 to 240 characters and no control characters (Sonnet, checked, Atlas lessons.py:29-30)
  - passSessionIds keeps 30 ids, so pass sessions older than 30 days count in the day-45 before-window (Sonnet, SKILL.md:68)
  - The skill makes the model do date maths and add counts; a tool field could do it (Fable, SKILL.md:51,64)
- Not shown before {status: question}
  - The 60-day read limit, and `otherSamples`, which the skill never reads (Fable, sessionContextServer.ts:238)
  - Atlas judges a lesson after 5 days or 20 calls; Nimbalyst waits 15 days (Sonnet, checked, Atlas lessons.py:25-26)
  - Atlas holds agent-written lessons as quarantined until the owner approves (Sonnet, checked, Atlas lessons.py:5,21)
  - Atlas also has secret and injection filters, a pass lease, a queue tidy and lesson packs (Fable, Hermes source on disk)
- Rule 1 {status: done}
  - resultText stays hand-written: the runtime package does not export extractToolResultText (both)

## Already on this machine {color: purple}
- memory-spike learn
  > Writes "failed command, then working command" lessons. No measurement, no retirement.
- nimbalyst-coach
  > Reads session signals and recommends changes. No failure classes, no verdicts.
